              "name": "tea",
              "externalId": "550"
            },
            "kind": "issue",
            "number": "1032"
          },
          "id": "1811077"
        },
        "body": "Before verifying: is tea being retired in favor of gt? If so, will the Gitea web UI follow? The Code dropdown still offers \"Tea CLI\" (`tea clone owner/repo`), even on https://gitea.com/gitea/cli, whose README points to `gt repo clone`.\r\n\r\nAs for this issue, it does not reproduce in gt built from main, tested against a disposable Gitea 1.26.4 (web on :3000, SSH on :2222):\r\n\r\n- `gt auth login --host http://localhost:3000` stores no ssh_host; the HTTP port is not copied.\r\n- A `git@localhost:owner/repo` remote resolves to the instance without any setting.\r\n- An `ssh://git@localhost:2222/...` remote fails with a hint to run `gt config set ssh_host localhost:2222 --host http://localhost:3000`, and resolves after that.\r\n- `gt repo clone` over SSH uses the API's ssh_url (`-p 2222`), not :3000."
      },
